{
  "name": "Wet Age-Related Macular Degeneration",
  "remarks": [
    "This module models wet (neovascular) age-related macular degeneration (AMD),",
    "a serious eye condition that causes rapid vision loss in the central field of vision.",
    "Wet AMD accounts for about 10-15% of all AMD cases but causes 90% of severe vision loss.",
    "It typically affects people over 50, with increasing prevalence with age.",
    "The module includes risk factors, progression from dry AMD, diagnostic procedures,",
    "and current treatment modalities including anti-VEGF therapy.",
    "References: AAO Retina/Vitreous Panel. Preferred Practice Pattern Guidelines.",
    "Age-Related Macular Degeneration. San Francisco, CA: American Academy of Ophthalmology; 2019.",
    "",
    "Remediation notes (module-audit-remediation, task 3.6):",
    " - Dry AMD onset was previously an age-tiered 5-25% chance PER 1-3 YEAR pass, compounding at",
    "   every re-roll (Age_Based_AMD_Risk -> No_AMD_Development -> loop) and pushing cumulative",
    "   incidence past 90% by age 85 -- roughly 10x the ~8-11% lifetime early-AMD prevalence reported",
    "   for a 55+ cohort (e.g. Beaver Dam Eye Study, Klein et al.). Replaced with a flat 0.8%/year",
    "   hazard (Dry_AMD_Annual_Roll) starting at age 55 (Dry_AMD_Age_Guard), checked on an exact",
    "   1-year Delay so no interval-compounding correction is needed (p_pass = p_annual when",
    "   Delta t = 1 year). This is a simplified flat-hazard calibration target, not a literal fit to",
    "   the age-stratified epidemiology curve, and is intentionally conservative (real incidence",
    "   rises with age); documented here so nobody downstream mistakes it for a SEER-grade rate.",
    " - Dry-to-wet conversion was a single one-shot roll after a random 1-5 year monitoring delay,",
    "   and its \"no conversion\" branch (No_AMD_Development, shared with the dry-onset loop above)",
    "   looped back into the DRY-onset check instead of re-checking wet conversion -- so a diagnosed",
    "   dry-AMD patient who didn't convert on the first roll could be re-diagnosed with dry AMD a",
    "   second time. Replaced with its own ongoing annual hazard (Wet_Conversion_Wait ->",
    "   Wet_Conversion_Risk_Check), moderate tier 1.5%/year (the brief's target rate), with modest",
    "   smoking/family-history stratification (low 1.2%/yr, high 2.5%/yr) retained from the original",
    "   risk-factor assessment logic -- broadly consistent with the ~1-3%/year annual conversion",
    "   rates reported across AMD natural-history cohorts.",
    " - Dry AMD was previously recorded via a bare ConditionOnset with no encounter open at all",
    "   (HealthRecord.currentEncounter falls back to the last encounter that happened to be open at",
    "   that simulated instant, or synthesizes a same-instant wellness encounter -- neither reflects",
    "   an actual visit). Now recorded inside a closed ambulatory encounter",
    "   (Dry_AMD_Diagnosis_Encounter / End_Dry_AMD_Diagnosis_Encounter).",
    " - Anti-VEGF treatment previously stopped for good after the 3-injection loading phase",
    "   (Loading_Phase_Wait capped injection_count < 3 and never returned to dosing afterward --",
    "   every treated patient reverted to observation-only follow-up for the rest of their life).",
    "   Replaced with an ongoing q4-8-week maintenance loop (Anti_VEGF_Maintenance_Wait ->",
    "   Anti_VEGF_Maintenance_Visit -> ... -> loop), matching AAO PPP treat-and-extend / fixed-",
    "   interval anti-VEGF regimens, which continue indefinitely rather than for a fixed 3 doses.",
    " - aflibercept/ranibizumab/bevacizumab RxCUIs were RxNorm SCDCs (ingredient+strength",
    "   components, no dose form) rather than dispensable SCDs: 1232151 (\"aflibercept 40 MG/ML\") ->",
    "   1232154 (SCD \"0.05 ML aflibercept 40 MG/ML Injection\", maps to HCPCS J0178); 643191",
    "   (\"ranibizumab 10 MG/ML\") -> 643193 (SCD \"0.05 ML ranibizumab 10 MG/ML Injection\", maps to",
    "   HCPCS J2778, added to export/rxnorm_hcpcs_map.json by this task -- it was not previously",
    "   scanned); 437105 (\"bevacizumab 25 MG/ML\") -> 1657066 (SCD \"4 ML bevacizumab 25 MG/ML",
    "   Injection\", maps to HCPCS J9035 -- the code real-world claims use for off-label intravitreal",
    "   Avastin, since there is no distinct FDA-approved intravitreal bevacizumab HCPCS code). All",
    "   three verified via RxNav rxcui/{id}/historystatus."
  ],
  "states": {
    "Initial": {
      "type": "Initial",
      "direct_transition": "Age_Guard"
    },
    "Age_Guard": {
      "type": "Guard",
      "allow": {
        "condition_type": "Age",
        "operator": ">=",
